NNAAMMEE
       pbmmake - create a blank bitmap of a specified size


SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       ppbbmmmmaakkee [--wwhhiittee|--bbllaacckk|--ggrraayy] _w_i_d_t_h _h_e_i_g_h_t

       You can abbreviate any option to its shortest unique prefix.



DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       ppbbmmmmaakkee  produces a PBM image of the specified width and height, either
       all black, all white, or a dithered gray.  The default is white.


OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       In addition to the options common to all programs  based  on  libnetpbm
       (most notably --qquuiieett, see
        Common  Options  ⟨index.html#commonoptions⟩  ), ppbbmmmmaakkee recognizes the
       following command line options:



       --wwhhiittee

       --bbllaacckk

       --ggrraayy

              In addition to the usual --wwhhiittee and --bbllaacckk, this program  imple‐
              ments  --ggrraayy.  This gives a simple 50% gray pattern with 1's and
              0's alternating.

              With none of the above specified, the output image will  be  en‐
              tirely white.




